{{- /*
product_add_ons.gohtml edits a product's add-ons (ADR 0232).

The list is a textarea holding one variant per line, by its SKU or its id, in
the order the storefront shows them. A SKU is what an operator knows; a picker
over every variant would not fit a catalog of fifty thousand. The module
replaces the list whole and refuses it whole, and the form comes back with what
was typed and the module's sentence naming the line to fix.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<p><a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">← Back to the product</a></p>

<h1>Add-ons of {{ .Product.Title }}</h1>
{{ if .Error }}<p role="alert">{{ .Error }}</p>{{ end }}

<form method="post" action="{{ .ActionPath }}">
  <label>Add-ons (one variant per line)
    <textarea name="add_ons" rows="8">{{ .Text }}</textarea>
  </label>
  <p>Each line is a variant of another product — an engraving, a gift wrap — by
  its SKU or its id, in the order the storefront shows them; at most {{ .Limit }}.
  A variant of a draft, or of a product sold in another channel, can be listed:
  the storefront leaves it out until it can show it. An empty list takes every
  add-on off.</p>
  <button type="submit">Save</button>
  <a href="{{ .CancelPath }}">Cancel</a>
</form>
{{ end }}
